import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 449 | Dragon Ball · Goku vs. Tang San: Predation Comparison of Dragon Ball and Douluo","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 449 | Dragon Ball · Goku vs. Tang San: Predation Comparison of Dragon Ball and Douluo","no":449,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Tang San","Douluo Continent","Predation Comparison","Killing-for-Level","Comparison"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","17-Plane Transcendent Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0449_模块2-龙珠-悟空vs唐三-龙珠与斗罗的掠夺对比.md","filePath":"en/0449_模块2-龙珠-悟空vs唐三-龙珠与斗罗的掠夺对比.md"}'),a={name:"en/0449_模块2-龙珠-悟空vs唐三-龙珠与斗罗的掠夺对比.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,u,h){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-449-dragon-ball-·-goku-vs-tang-san-predation-comparison-of-dragon-ball-and-douluo" tabindex="-1">Entry 449 | Dragon Ball · Goku vs. Tang San: Predation Comparison of Dragon Ball and Douluo <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-449-dragon-ball-·-goku-vs-tang-san-predation-comparison-of-dragon-ball-and-douluo" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 449 | Dragon Ball · Goku vs. Tang San: Predation Comparison of Dragon Ball and Douluo&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 18 · Cross-Protagonist Comparison 5) | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 19, 17</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-two-kinds-of-predation-which-is-cleaner" tabindex="-1">Introduction: two kinds of predation, which is &quot;cleaner&quot;? <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-two-kinds-of-predation-which-is-cleaner" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: two kinds of predation, which is &quot;cleaner&quot;?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang San (<em>Douluo Continent</em>) is institutionalized predation&#39;s representative: he wrote &quot;kill to get spirit rings&quot; into every realm&#39;s legal promotion procedure, enfeoffed Divine Realm positions by family private grant. Goku is innocent-type predation&#39;s representative: he does not actively predate, but his growth is built on &quot;near-death revival + enemies as EXP packs.&quot; Both predate, but Tang San&#39;s predation is &quot;open rules,&quot; Goku&#39;s predation is &quot;hidden rules.&quot; This entry, by the law-first axiom and anti-predation axiom, compares these two predations&#39; structural differences.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Goku&#39;s waste</strong>: Zeno-tier aptitude for personal combat; civilization zero institutional spillover</li><li><strong>Tang San&#39;s waste</strong>: God-King-tier aptitude for enfeoffing the whole family as gods; the mortal world loses god-tier feedback</li><li><strong>Comparison</strong>: both&#39;s energy not truly benefited Myriad Ranks — Goku for fighting, Tang San for enfeoffing his own</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Goku&#39;s world</strong>: strong one absent = collapse; disasters relied on wish rollback</li><li><strong>Tang San&#39;s world</strong>: spirit-beast stock exhausted; Divine Realm closed and self-defended; pantheon = family</li><li><strong>Common lesion</strong>: both&#39;s civilizations built on consuming stock — Goku consumes Myriad Ranks&#39; blood; Tang San consumes spirit beasts&#39; lives</li></ul><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Goku&#39;s predation</strong>: innocent type — he is truly kind, but his growth needs &quot;a stronger villain appears&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang San&#39;s predation</strong>: institutional type — he wrote predation into rules; killing = leveling, divine position = private property</li><li><strong>Comparison</strong>: Tang San&#39;s predation is more thorough than Goku&#39;s — Goku at least does not actively kill; Tang San wrote killing into every realm&#39;s breakthrough; but Goku&#39;s predation is more concealed than Tang San&#39;s — Tang San&#39;s predation readers can see clearly; Goku&#39;s predation wrapped in &quot;hot-blood&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Goku</th><th>Tang San</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Predation type</td><td>Innocent type (enemies as EXP packs)</td><td>Institutional type (killing = leveling)</td><td>Anti-predation axiom</td></tr><tr><td>Evolution path</td><td>Near-death revival + anger transformation</td><td>Hunt spirit beasts + absorb spirit rings</td><td>Path D · artificial Dao-law spirit rings + safe deduction</td></tr><tr><td>Divine position / ultimate</td><td>God of Destruction—Angel—Zeno</td><td>God-King family private grant</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republicanism; god-tier qualification public exam</td></tr><tr><td>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</td><td>High (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</td><td>High (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</td><td>Extremely low (network)</td></tr><tr><td>Common way out</td><td>Let Goku make ki theory public</td><td>Let Tang San abandon killing-for-level</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republican co-build</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates two worlds — Dragon Ball cosmos and Douluo cosmos</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;Goku makes ki theory public,&quot; &quot;Tang San switches to Path D artificial Dao-law spirit rings&quot; controls</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count Myriad-Ranks casualty rate, spirit-beast population survival, civilization long-term construction rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Two Predation Modes Comparison Report</em>, quantifying &quot;innocent-type predation&quot; vs. &quot;institutional-type predation&quot; which is closer to the anti-predation axiom</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Dragon Ball self-consistency: low</strong> (number inflation, multi-line retcon)</li><li><strong>Douluo self-consistency: low</strong> (spirit rings late padding; Divine Realm multi-arc mutually overturned)</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: both = high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</li><li><strong>Common lesion</strong>: both&#39;s civilizations built on consuming stock; no incremental development</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: both&#39;s energy not truly benefited Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Goku plunders enemies as leveling fuel; Tang San plunders spirit beasts as spirit rings</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least does not kill; Tang San wrote killing into rules</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: both worlds&#39; Myriad Ranks are &quot;consumed/protected&quot; objects</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: both predatory civilizations cannot truly move toward open multiverse</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku and Tang San are the predation lineage&#39;s two poles: one innocently stands on predatory foundation, one consciously writes predation into rules. Neither is &quot;evil,&quot; but both&#39;s systems make Myriad Ranks pay blood price. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is the anti-predation axiom — develop increment, do not consume stock, do not take killing-predation as evolution path. Whether innocent type or institutional type, as long as still consuming stock, still one step from Myriad-Ranks symbiosis.</p><p>One more layer: Tang San&#39;s predation at least has a clear &quot;bill&quot; — kill one spirit beast for one level; readers can calculate the price. Goku&#39;s predation is instead more concealed: he does not actively kill spirit beasts, but every time he gets stronger he needs &quot;a stronger villain appears,&quot; and behind every villain is a destroyed city, a slaughtered race. Tang San&#39;s predation is written in rules; Goku&#39;s predation is hidden in narrative — what readers see is &quot;Goku got angry again&quot;; what they do not see is &quot;to make Goku angry, the writer killed a city&#39;s worth of people.&quot; From predation&#39;s concealment, Goku is actually harder to identify than Tang San.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · Goku vs. Tang San · predation comparison of Dragon Ball and Douluo described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./448_模块2-龙珠-悟空vs石昊-龙珠与完美的个人主义对比.html">Entry 448 · Goku vs. Shi Hao</a> · <a href="./450_模块2-龙珠-悟空vs纪宁-龙珠与莽荒的穿越者对比.html">Entry 450 · Goku vs. Ji Ning</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',26)])])}const p=i(a,[["render",s]]);export{c as __pageData,p as default};
